  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;MOYALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moyale is a town in Ethiopia with varying population estimates and demographic characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL STATISTICAL AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Central Statistical Agency provides population estimates and census data for various regions in Ethiopia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHIOPIAN CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ethiopian census is a periodic survey conducted to gather demographic data on the population of Ethiopia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GARRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Garre is a clan belonging to the Somali people and is one of the major groups in Woreda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Garre is one of the major ethnic groups in Moyale, along with other groups such as Degodia and Hawadle."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BORENA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Borena is another ethnic group mentioned in relation to Moyale, alongside the Garre."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GABBRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gabbra is a small nomadic group with cultural similarities to the Borena Oromo and is a minority in Woreda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Gabbra is a small nomadic group with cultural similarities to the Borena Oromo, living in the woreda."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGODIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degodia is a clan belonging to the Somali people and is one of the major groups in Woreda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Degodia is one of the major ethnic groups in the woreda, alongside the Garre and Hawadle."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAWADLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hawadle is a clan belonging to the Somali people and is one of the major groups in Woreda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hawadle is one of the major ethnic groups in the woreda, alongside the Garre and Degodia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZONE AVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Zone average refers to the general population statistics for the region, used for comparison."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBAN DWELLERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urban dwellers are individuals living in urban areas, as opposed to rural areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASTORALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pastoralists are a subgroup of the total population and make up 39.79% of the population."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pastoralists are individuals engaged in nomadic herding and livestock management."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSLIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RELIGION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muslim is the predominant religion among the inhabitants of the woreda, according to the 2007 census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2005 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2005 census provides population estimates for Moyale, including detailed breakdowns by gender and ethnicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1994 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1994 census reports population data for Moyale, including estimates for parts of the town not counted in the official census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2007 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2007 Census conducted by the Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia provided detailed demographic information for Woreda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 2007 census conducted by the Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia (CSA) provides detailed population data for the woreda."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1997 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1997 national census reports population data for the woreda, including estimates for various ethnic groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUT-MIGRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Out-migration has led to a significant decrease in population since the 1994 census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECONOMIC DECLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Economic decline has contributed to the significant decrease in population since the 1994 census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOREDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Woreda is a geographical area with a defined population and demographic characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Woreda is a lower administrative division in Ethiopia, often corresponding to a district or county."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMALI PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somali people are the primary ethnic group in Woreda, including the Garre, Degodia, and Hawadle clans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Somali people include various ethnic groups such as the Garre, Borena, and Gabbra."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National censuses provide comprehensive demographic data for the entire country or specific regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RURAL KEBELES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rural kebeles are small administrative units within a woreda, often corresponding to villages or hamlets."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASTORALISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pastoralism is a traditional way of life involving nomadic herding and livestock management."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOMADIC GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nomadic groups are communities that move from place to place, often following seasonal patterns for grazing."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OROMO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Oromo are a large ethnic group in Ethiopia, including sub-groups such as the Borena."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL STATISTICAL AGENCY OF ETHIOPIA (CSA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia (CSA) is responsible for conducting censuses and collecting demographic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia is responsible for conducting censuses and collecting demographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BORENA OROMO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Borena Oromo is a group with cultural similarities to the Gabbra and is mentioned in relation to the Gabbra."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OROMIA ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oromia administration is the governing body that oversees the disputed areas based on the referendum results."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHIOPIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethiopia is the country where Woreda is located and where the Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia operates."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL POPULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total population refers to the overall number of people living in Woreda."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Men are part of the total population and make up 138,790 individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Women are part of the total population and make up 115,347 individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBAN INHABITANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urban inhabitants are not part of the total population, indicating a rural setting."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSLIMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RELIGION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"99.4% of the population identifies as Muslim."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1997 NATIONAL CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1997 national census reported a total population for this woreda, providing historical demographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISPUTED AREAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disputed areas are regions within Woreda that have been subject to political debate or contestation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REFERENDUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The referendum resulted in about 80% of the disputed areas falling under the Oromia administration, despite allegations of voting irregularities."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOTING IRREGULARITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Voting irregularities were alleged during the referendum, affecting the validity of the results."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OROMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oromia is a region in Ethiopia that administers the disputed areas based on the referendum results."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0490-c6a7a009b76b</data>
    </node>
